The metric oscillates with period 2π in Wick rotation angle. If the Wick rotation angle is physical, this periodicity should be observable.

**Test:** Look for periodic oscillations in precision measurements of spacetime.

### 9.2 The Big Bang Every Planck Time

The big bang happens every Planck time. This is 10⁻⁴³ seconds.

**Test:** Look for Planck-scale periodicity in high-energy experiments.

### 9.3 The Two Helicity States

The derivation relies on the photon having exactly two helicity states. If the photon had more, the derivation would fail.

**Test:** Measure the number of photon helicity states to high precision.

